  "readmeFile": "readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.1-preview.33\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.33 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.32\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.32 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.31\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.31 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.30\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.30 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.29\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.29 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.28\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.28 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.27\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.27 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.26\n- Synchronized package version with the preview.26 release.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.25\n- Fixes Mac Catalyst. The package now ships a net10.0-maccatalyst asset and delegates to Auth.Apple on that head. Previously a net10.0-maccatalyst consumer resolved the plain net10.0 browser asset, so UseUno() threw UnoFirebaseAuthException at startup.\n- Mac Catalyst defines MACCATALYST (and __IOS__), not IOS. The per-head dispatch is now IOS || MACCATALYST in both the using block and the registration branch; fixing only the asset or only the symbol leaves the failure in place.\n\nv1.0.1-preview.24\n- Adds the Uno Platform integration for Firebase Authentication. UseUno() delegates to the platform package that matches the Uno head the application is running on.\n- The package references no Uno package and stays framework-independent, exactly as the .Maui packages reference no MAUI package. The head is detected at runtime, so the browser and Skia-desktop heads share the plain net10.0 asset.\n- Fails fast with UnoFirebaseAuthException on the Skia desktop head, including Linux, because FireForNet ships no desktop integration packages.",
